% F48-FRADIX: DEFECT 48.  .EFIX SCALES BY POWERS OF 10, BUT .# TOOK ITS
% DIGITS IN THE RADIX, SO IN HEX 255 PRINTED AS 414.7AE1, THE EXPONENT CAME
% OUT IN HEX, AND IN OCTAL A 9 GAVE "OUTPUT CONVERSION ERROR."  PATCHED,
% FLOAT OUTPUT IS DECIMAL IN ANY RADIX, AS .= AND FLOAT INPUT ARE.
FLOAT< DECIMAL
() I_ABORT ABORT !
HEX
"|" MSG 255. .<#> TYPE "|" MSG 255. 8 2 F= "|" MSG 1.E20 C 2 E= "|" MSG CR
"|" MSG 8 RADIX ! 99. 6 1 F= "|" MSG CR
DECIMAL
12345 = CR
